From 32b037a68f9eb0ab32ff296e65dad2415b162968 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 00:48:44 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] fix(kanban): park pin ignores a text-named shared
 checkout; untracked remote branches proven by test

11-12 18:45Z: 7 of 9 open pool_pinned park pins on the hub board were false.

Class A (5 cards, worker-2, "dirty worktree /home/ubuntu/.hermes/hermes-agent"):
- Why 1: kanban_park_pin pinned each card because kanban_move_pool.tree_state()
  returned that state; every payload has the live checkout in `trees`.
- Why 2: card_trees() adds trees named in the card's text. Core cards name
  ~/.hermes/hermes-agent, so the gateway's shared live checkout counted as the
  card's own tree.
- Why 3: one stray untracked file there (cache-sizes.txt) made it dirty, so every
  core card parking on worker-2 pinned to it; a false p1000 pin made worker-2's
  core rollout yield.
- Root: park-pin treats a text-named shared main checkout as a tree the card owns.
  PR #1681 added linked_text_only=True for move departures only.

Class B (2 cards, worker-6, "unpushed commits in <workspace>/<tree>"):
- Why 1: _worktree_has_unpushed_commits runs `git log HEAD --not --remotes`, which
  reads local tracking refs only.
- Why 2: the workspace clone tracks only origin/state and HEAD was pushed to
  another branch name, so no tracking ref holds it.
- Root: the pushed-ness check trusted local tracking refs. 82b88332ad made
  tree_state ask the remote when HEAD equals a remote tip, and 41ae5143f0 /
  77a71becc9 (landed while this PR waited) refresh untracked remote heads with a
  bounded fetch, which covers a remote tip that contains HEAD. This commit keeps
  that code and adds the single-branch-clone regression tests for it.

Not caught: the park-pin tests used per-card trees only; none covered a dirty
shared checkout named in text or a single-branch clone pushed under another name.

Fix:
- Park pin (pin and unpin) passes linked_text_only=True. Text-named trees (and a
  pin's recorded `trees`) count only when they are linked worktrees or clones at
  a per-card location (~/code/_wt/<slug>, the other worktree globs), so the live
  core checkout and other shared main checkouts never pin a card, and an old
  false pin lifts at the card's next park. Moves (#1681) get the same per-card
  location rule, which only widens what they protect.
- Remote timeout (ls-remote and the refresh fetch) 20 s -> 10 s; any
  error/timeout still fails toward pinning. _worktree_has_unpushed_commits stays
  local-only on purpose: GC and worktree exit call it per tree with tight
  timeouts, and tree_state layers the remote check on top (park and move both go
  through tree_state).
- pool_pinned payload records `check` (dirty/unpushed) and `tree`.

Tests (tests/hermes_cli/test_kanban_pool_queue.py):
- dirty shared-checkout stand-in named in text + clean pushed owned worktree:
  park does not pin; an old pin naming the live checkout lifts.
- dirty text-named linked worktree still pins; event has check/tree.
- single-branch clone (tracks only state) with HEAD on wt/x, then the remote
  branch moved past HEAD: tree_state None, park keeps the pool, move refuses
  pool_keeps_pushed.
- fail safe: a HEAD on no remote, an unreachable remote and an ls-remote
  timeout (<= 10 s) all still pin.
- test_remote_failure_pins_without_reading_stdin's clone moves to a per-card
  location (~/code/_wt/unreachable): a clone named only in text elsewhere no
  longer counts for park.

Card: t_01a1d145c441f2bd
